WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:29.000
Dark Magician User
Pandora

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.370
Stop joking around!

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:41.650
That lame card doesn't meet my definition of a rare card!

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:46.650
But you were fine with this ante card before we started the duel.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.630
I changed my mind.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:52.660
The loser has to obey the winner!

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:54.750
What?  Please don't...

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:55.660
Whatever!

00:01:58.750 --> 00:01:59.650
Warning!

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:01.770
What's with this kid?

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:06.150
I'm Battle City commissioner Mokuba Kaiba.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:12.280
I'm in charge of quickly resolving issues in the tournament.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:14.780
Don't interfere with my rules!

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:18.280
If you can't follow the rules, you're not a duelist!

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:19.660
What?

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:22.080
What a selfish duelist.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.560
What did you say?

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:28.850
Brother!

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:30.700
Seto Kaiba!

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:36.200
Insulting my little brother is the same as insulting Kaiba Corporation.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.710
Are you willing to pay the price?

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:40.570
What do you mean?

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.600
Wow!  Incredible!

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.580
They're all rare cards!

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:54.150
I challenge you to a duel right now.

00:02:54.470 --> 00:03:00.160
But you must use cards in that briefcase to strengthen your weak deck.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.000
You'll regret this.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:11.750
Thanks to your rare cards, I built the strongest deck possible.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:12.970
Cards are power!

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.720
I'm 100% sure that I won't lose!

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.780
Let's go!  Duel!

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.620
I'll show you a god.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:26.790
This is real power!

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:07.990
I have one god.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:10.140
There are two left.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:18.800
When I find those cards in the city, I'll complete my supreme God Deck, and everyone will kneel before me.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:24.840
Yugi, wait for me on my road of battle.

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:31.620
You found a lead on Obelisk?

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.770
Yes.  North C block in Domino City.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:37.110
The owner of the card is...

00:04:37.550 --> 00:04:39.130
...Seto Kaiba.

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:41.130
That's what I thought.

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:43.660
But how did Kaiba get it?

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:45.320
It's not hard to imagine.

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:49.930
He started this tournament because he acquired a God Card.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.480
This tournament is a ritual to gather the Gods.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.650
I know you're behind this.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:13.120
Unlock it.

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:36.080
Marik, my Millennium Necklace allowed me to see what you would do.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:42.590
Our family has protected the Valley of the Kings for 3,000 years.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:46.320
You're wasting the sacrifices of our ancestors.

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:48.660
They sacrificed for what?

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.330
Someone eventually had to get rid of this tradition.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:58.190
I will gather the three God Cards and acquire the title of the Pharaoh.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:02.370
And I will free our family from our cursed destiny!

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:05.300
You're betraying our family!

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:07.610
I can't let you pass.

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:10.610
Move out of my way.

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:15.120
Are you willing to use your Millennium Rod on me?

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:18.120
I can if it's for our family's future.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:20.920
Even on you, sister.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:32.760
Sister, I knew you had the final card.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:38.620
You were guided by the Millennium Necklace's hazy glimpse of the future.

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:44.530
You saw that giving Obelisk to Seto Kaiba would lead him to creating this tournament.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:52.660
You saw that the gods would have my destiny and his destiny intersect in Domino City.

00:06:53.150 --> 00:06:59.160
But in the end, I will hold all the God Cards.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:02.170
And the title of the Pharaoh.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:08.560
Shall we send the Rare Hunters to North block to go after Kaiba?

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:10.670
No, let him go.

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:13.680
I've found the Pharaoh.

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:17.600
Get Pandora the Illusionist ready to duel.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:18.360
Yes, sir.

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:27.050
I'll come back later.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:30.660
I want to see how Yugi and Jonouchi are doing.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:31.700
Umm...

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.580
Honda, I have a request.

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:40.160
When I remove these bandages, I want you to show me around Domino City.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:41.170
Domino City?

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:46.410
Yes.  The first thing I want to see is my brother dueling.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.150
Leave it to me.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:53.820
I hope Shizuka can remove her bandages soon.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:54.380
Yeah.

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:57.830
You must work hard for Shizuka, my student.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:58.890
I know.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:01.700
We'll go look for Yugi.

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:03.080
Okay.  See ya.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:20.440
Partner, this card represents Jonouchi's courage.

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:25.950
Jonouchi is trying to get this card back using his own strength.

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:29.950
Jonouchi will keep winning in Battle City, right?

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:31.080
Yeah.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:37.460
When the time comes, I'll accept his challenge because Katsuya Jonouchi will be a true duelist.

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:44.170
Regardless of who loses that duel, it will be engraved in our memories forever.

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:48.660
Just like my memories of playing games with Grandpa long ago.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:51.730
Oh yeah.

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:56.060
My other self has no memories of the time before we met.

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:06.680
Is that a Rare Hunter?

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:10.110
Is he calling me?

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.600
Isn't that Yugi?

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:27.780
Huh?  Where?

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:31.150
Yugi!

00:09:58.770 --> 00:09:59.770
Yugi!

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:07.280
Yugi!

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:10.860
Where did you go, Yugi?

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:12.190
Yugi, answer us!

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:14.690
What?

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:15.920
Brother!

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:21.430
The surveillance center said that Yugi Muto's ID signal vanished!

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:22.430
Yugi vanished?

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.080
Is it the Ghouls?

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:27.660
Mokuba, have them investigate this thoroughly!

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:34.620
The Duel Disk constantly emits an ID signal.

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:39.260
If we can't detect it, he's in a location where the signal is blocked.

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:42.360
Like the basement of a building.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:01.970
My duelist data?

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:04.470
What's this?

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:11.330
What?

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:16.270
I've been waiting for you, Yugi.

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:20.990
You will duel my master Pandora.

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:22.280
Pandora?

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:27.230
There is only one person in the world who can truly wield the mightiest Magician card!

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:31.500
You will learn that this person is Pandora the Illusionist!

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:36.000
Enough tricks!  Show yourself, Rare Hunter!

00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:43.420
Welcome.  I'm the second Rare Hunter, Pandora.

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:46.680
The illusionist who uses Dark Magician.

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:08.740
Welcome.  I'm the second Rare Hunter, Pandora.

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:12.020
The illusionist who uses Dark Magician.

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:15.180
You use Dark Magician?

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:21.180
Yugi, I know that you also use Dark Magician to defeat many duelists.

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:24.820
But I'm the master of magicians.

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:27.690
No one can defeat my Dark Magician!

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:29.340
Are you sure?

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:35.430
From among many cards, a duelist chooses ones that he believes in to build his deck.

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:38.640
But the cards also choose the duelist.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:46.170
When these two hearts unite in trust, the cards unleash their true power.

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:49.180
A Rare Hunter doesn't have a heart of a duelist!

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:53.140
Okay.  I accept your challenge, Pandora.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:56.300
My Dark Magician will defeat you!

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:05.360
I'm honored that you're graciously accepting this duel.

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:07.940
This room is too small.

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:12.220
I've prepared a special Duel Ring.  Come this way.

00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:14.670
Duel Ring?

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.380
This way.

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:24.340
Before I invited you, Marik warned me not to bore you.

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:28.750
Marik?  The leader of the Ghouls who holds a Millennium Item?

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:30.800
Where is he?

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:32.250
Answer me, Pandora!

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:35.040
I wonder where he is...

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:38.980
Maybe he's nearby.  Maybe he's in here.

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:46.520
Marik can take over people's minds and control them.

00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:48.770
Is he controlling Pandora?

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:51.080
Please enter.

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:53.560
This is our Duel Ring.

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:58.480
This is Pandora's room.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:06.840
Do you like the architecture?

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:11.730
An illusionist's job is to manipulate cards and occasionally create nightmares.

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:16.730
This is the perfect stage for a duel between Dark Magicians.

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:24.000
We'll use my Solid Vision System because I don't want Kaiba Corporation to know about this place.

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:29.980
Let's carefully shuffle our decks.

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:35.500
Shuffling shotgun-style can damage your cards.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.760
I'm used to shuffling this way.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:41.870
I'll cut your deck.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.070
Go ahead.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:48.100
There's an old saying among gamblers:

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:52.200
"Trust your friends, but cut his deck of cards."

00:14:53.520 --> 00:14:54.700
Friend?

00:14:56.360 --> 00:14:58.210
I can never be your friend.

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:00.610
That's too bad.

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:09.660
But since we're going to duel, I want you to have fun so that we can deepen our friendship.

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:14.540
Please enjoy this nightmarish show!

00:15:16.780 --> 00:15:17.690
What?

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.680
Yes, I'm locked up too.

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:24.430
Neither of us can flee.

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:31.950
You'll now witness Pandora the Illusionist's once-in-a-generation escape show!

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:35.440
What?

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:44.240
These buzzsaws are used in large-scale magic tricks.

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:47.690
You now know the rules of this duel.

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:52.690
There are numbers written on the saw rails.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:54.920
They're life points!

00:15:54.920 --> 00:15:58.200
As our life points fall towards 0, the buzzsaws come closer!

00:15:58.200 --> 00:15:59.400
That's right.

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:01.820
The loser gets chopped up in this game.

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:05.130
Look at your feet.

00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:08.710
We each have one.

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:10.440
What's this box?

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:15.940
Inside is a key that will unlock our leg straps.

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:22.880
The box displays the opponent's life points, and it will open when the points reach 0.

00:16:22.880 --> 00:16:27.190
In other words, only the winner can escape.

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:28.690
How dare you!

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:35.820
The god Zeus put every catastrophe inside Pandora's Box.

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:40.120
No one was allowed to open it, but when she did...

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:45.210
...all the evil emerged from the box, hurting everyone.

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:49.800
But one thing was left inside the box - hope.

00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:56.120
The key inside the box represents our final hope.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:01.460
This is fun?

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:06.230
You think it's fun to fight for our lives?

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:09.250
Yes.  Because I'm going to win.

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:11.090
You're rotten!

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:18.480
I'll show you how a true duelist battles!

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:24.770
Duel!

00:17:31.770 --> 00:17:33.310
I go first!

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:36.710
I draw five cards.

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:43.000
I already have Dark Magician in my hand.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:46.150
Or should I say that I made it come to my hand.

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:51.840
An illusionist has over a thousand techniques to control his cards.

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:55.980
Getting the card I want into my hand is easy to do.

00:17:56.420 --> 00:18:00.220
I used a technique called the "stripper."

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:07.420
By cutting a strip off a card, it's now a different size than the rest of the cards.

00:18:08.260 --> 00:18:12.120
By stripping my three Dark Magician cards...

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:17.280
...I can always get a Dark Magician on top of my deck when I cut my deck.

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:26.530
Yugi, this game of death will show you why it's foolish to challenge an illusionist in a card battle.

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:28.030
Here I go!

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:29.460
It's my turn!

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:31.960
I set one card.

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:38.000
Then I summon Alpha The Magnet Warrior in defense position.

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:39.990
I end my turn.

00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:42.490
My turn.

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:45.260
Legion the Fiend Jester in defense position.

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:55.510
If I summon another monster, I can tribute them to summon Dark Magician.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:56.960
My turn!

00:19:03.850 --> 00:19:07.250
Pandora, I'll play a spell card this turn.

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:08.250
A spell card?

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:09.830
The card is...

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:13.490
Card Destruction!

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:16.000
What?  Card Destruction?

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:18.760
We must discard our entire hands.

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:20.230
That includes you, Pandora!

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.370
Entire hand...

00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:25.960
I have to discard Dark Magician.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:30.710
I expected you to have Dark Magician in your hand.

00:19:30.840 --> 00:19:35.020
Since you're an illusionist, I had to be aware that you might cheat.

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:40.450
And I don't think someone who shuffles shotgun-style cares about his cards.

00:19:40.730 --> 00:19:44.590
I knew you wouldn't think twice about stripping your cards.

00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:46.950
No way...

00:19:46.950 --> 00:19:49.690
You knew and still accepted my challenge?

00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:53.980
My turn isn't over yet!

00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:56.560
I flip over my set card!

00:19:58.480 --> 00:20:00.200
Brain Control!

00:20:00.810 --> 00:20:02.270
Brain Control?

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:04.750
You're planning to control my monster?

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:16.830
I tribute Alpha The Magnet Warrior and Legion the Fiend Jester!

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:24.630
I summon Dark Magician!

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:31.670
I'll show you how much pain a card feels when it's stripped, Pandora!

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:35.910
He summoned Dark Magician before me!

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:39.450
If you want to have a dangerous game, I accept!

00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:43.690
But you should also be prepared to take the pain, Pandora!

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:47.420
Dark Magician, attack him directly!

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:54.860
Black Magic!

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:09.020
This attack lowered your life points to 1500.

00:21:09.020 --> 00:21:13.380
Now show me this once-in-a-generation show you were talking about.

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:21.480
You're pretty good.

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:25.890
But the real show is only getting started!

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:45.540
The breathtaking battle between Dark Magicians is evenly matched.

00:21:45.540 --> 00:21:50.320
But Pandora will do anything to win, even if it means stripping his cards.

00:21:50.320 --> 00:21:52.320
His attacks put Yugi in a pinch!

00:21:52.570 --> 00:21:57.970
Yugi says he'll battle to the end by believing in himself and his cards, but...

00:21:57.970 --> 00:22:01.520
Please, Dark Magician!  Live up to the trust that Yugi has in you!

00:22:02.270 --> 00:22:05.050
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Black Magic of the Soul

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:06.700
Duel, standby!

00:22:21.530 --> 00:22:26.030
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:26.830 --> 00:22:31.400
I feel like I've been here

00:22:31.940 --> 00:22:41.080
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:41.380 --> 00:22:52.590
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:55.460 --> 00:23:00.100
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:05.370
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:10.480
Will never change

00:23:11.140 --> 00:23:15.750
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:16.380 --> 00:23:20.950
To be who I am

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:26.190
I've kept searching for something

00:23:26.860 --> 00:23:30.900
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:30.900 --> 00:23:33.830
I learned that's the answer

00:23:34.630 --> 00:23:40.940
From now until forever...
